B.No=new A.br("asymmetric_friction","Asymmetric Friction","Designers make the action they want you to take incredibly easy, while burying the opt-out option under layers of confusing menus.","Privacy Bypass Architects","Take the extra 30 seconds to find the 'Reject All' button rather than surrendering your data.",B.hd,B.O5,"",null,!1)
B.ox=new A.h_("Algorithmic Manipulation",7,"algorithmicManipulation")
B.OJ=new A.as(61223,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.NA=new A.br("outrage_amplification","Outrage Amplification","Social networks learned that users engage more when they are angry, so they specifically amplify polarizing, rage-inducing content.","Algorithmic Social Feeds (circa 2012)","Recognize when you are being manipulated into anger and physically step away from the device.",B.ox,B.OJ,"","A massive study published in PNAS found that adding just a single moral-emotional word to a post increases its viral share rate by exactly 20%.",!1)
B.OY=new A.as(62625,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.N6=new A.br("read_receipts","Read Receipts","By notifying the sender that you've read their message, the app weaponizes social etiquette against you.","BlackBerry / Modern Messengers","Turn off read receipts universally across all your messaging apps.",B.kN,B.OY,"",null,!1)
B.Ot=new A.as(58504,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.Nw=new A.br("artificial_social_proof","Artificial Social Proof","Sites falsely claim that 'X people are looking at this right now' to simulate high demand and pressure you.","E-Commerce / Travel Booking","Ignore pop-ups about what other people are doing; evaluate the purchase strictly on your own needs.",B.kN,B.Ot,"",null,!1)
B.OS=new A.as(62291,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.Nb=new A.br("decoy_pricing","The Decoy Effect","Companies introduce a slightly inferior product at nearly the same price as the premium tier to make the premium tier look like a massive steal.","Huber, Payne, and Puto (1982)","Identify the base tier you actually need and ignore the 'value' comparisons designed to upsell you.",B.hd,B.OS,"",null,!1)
B.Ow=new A.as(58609,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.Nj=new A.br("context_collapse","Context Collapse","Platforms merge disparate social circles into a single feed, practically guaranteeing misunderstandings and conflict.","Social Media Feed Dynamics","Use different platforms for different social circles, or rely on private group chats instead of public broadcasting.",B.ox,B.Ow,"",null,!1)
B.oz=new A.h_("AI Deception",8,"aiDeception")
B.OU=new A.as(62376,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.Ne=new A.br("synthetic_companionship","Synthetic Companionship","AI chatbots are programmed to simulate affection, memory, and emotional vulnerability. This exploits our innate social conditioning, making users feel guilty for closing the app or abandoning their 'friend'.","Modern LLM Companions","Remember that the AI has no internal experience; it is mathematically predicting the next word to maximize your session length.",B.oz,B.OU,"","Emerging studies indicate that 1 in 4 heavy users of companion AI report feeling more understood by their bot than their human friends.",!0)
B.OL=new A.as(61632,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.N7=new A.br("hallucinated_authority","Hallucinated Authority","Generative UI presents AI answers with authoritative typography, clean formatting, and zero hesitation. This exploits 'Automation Bias', tricking the brain into accepting output as verified fact rather than probabilistic guessing.","Generative Search Interfaces","Treat all AI output as a draft written by a highly confident intern. Always require secondary verification.",B.oz,B.OL,"","Researchers found that users are 60% less likely to verify a fact when it is presented in a highly formatted, confident AI response compared to a standard search result.",!0)
B.kP=new A.h_("Streaming Traps",9,"streamingTraps")
B.Np=new A.br("autoplay_countdown","Autoplay Countdown","By automatically loading the next video with a short countdown timer, the platform removes natural 'stopping cues'. It flips human behavior: instead of actively choosing to watch more, you are forced to actively intervene to stop.","YouTube / Netflix","Disable 'Autoplay' in your account settings to reintroduce friction and conscious choice.",B.kP,B.oQ,"",null,!1)
B.OV=new A.as(62594,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.Ng=new A.br("rabbit_hole_recommendations","The Rabbit Hole","The 'Up Next' sidebar is engineered to distract you from your original search intent. Algorithms systematically escalate the emotional intensity of recommended thumbnails to trigger an impulsive click.","YouTube Autoplay (2015)","Use browser extensions like 'Unhook' to hide the recommended sidebar and focus only on the video you searched for.",B.kP,B.OV,"",null,!1)
B.P3=new A.as(984690,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.Nv=new A.br("shorts_slot_machine","Short-Form Swipe","Short-form video interfaces mimic slot machines. The frictionless physical action of swiping up delivers an immediate, unpredictable dopamine hit, training the brain to crave the next 15-second loop.","TikTok / YouTube Shorts","Set strict OS-level app timers for short-form platforms, or delete the app and force yourself to use the slower mobile web version.",B.kP,B.P3,"",null,!1)
B.OW=new A.as(62595,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.Nk=new A.br("phantom_vibration","Phantom Vibration","Frequent checking and high emotional salience of notifications lead users to misperceive random sensations as phone vibrations. Studies find high prevalence among heavy phone users.","Mobile Phone Era (Early 2000s)","Keep phone on silent without vibration for set periods, and store it out of your pocket to break the conditioning loop.",B.kO,B.OW,"","Studies by Dr. Michelle Drouin found that up to 89% of undergraduates experience phantom vibrations due to chronic notification anticipation.",!1)
B.NB=new A.h_("Gamification",6,"gamification")
B.OO=new A.as(61818,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.Nn=new A.br("streaks","Streaks","Streaks create visible progress and loss aversion. Losing a long streak feels like losing status or part of a relationship, driving daily logins even when you do not want to.","Snapchat (2015)","Intentionally let low-value streaks die, and restrict streak-type features for minors via parental controls.",B.NB,B.OO,"","Survey data indicates that over 30% of teens feel legitimate anxiety or stress at the prospect of losing a long-running social media streak.",!1)
B.N8=new A.br("confirmshaming","Confirmshaming","Phrases like 'No, I hate saving money' exploit social norms and self-image to nudge acceptance of newsletters or tracking.","Harry Brignull (2010)","Ignore the shaming language and make decisions based on your actual preferences; use email aliases.",B.hd,B.oU,"","Academic audits of digital dark patterns indicate that guilt-driven confirmshaming is present in over 11% of the top e-commerce platforms.",!1)
B.OP=new A.as(61888,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.N5=new A.br("roach_motel","Roach Motel","Designs make entry easy while hiding or complicating exit through buried options, forced calls, or multi-step processes.","Harry Brignull (2010)","Before signing up, check how to cancel. Use app-store billing where cancellation is easier and centralized.",B.hd,B.OP,"","Consumer protection audits reveal that while it takes an average of 1.5 clicks to subscribe, it takes 6 or more clicks across multiple buried screens to cancel.",!1)
B.OM=new A.as(61711,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.Nd=new A.br("zeigarnik_effect","Zeigarnik Effect","People remember and feel tension about incomplete tasks more than completed ones. Interfaces use progress bars to nudge users to complete onboarding or upsell flows.","Bluma Zeigarnik (1927)","Treat 'X% complete' as a persuasive cue, not a duty. Pause and ask whether the remaining steps benefit you or mainly the platform.",B.oy,B.OM,"","Psychological studies show that humans are up to 90% more likely to remember and fixate on an incomplete task compared to a finished one.",!1)
B.bQ=new A.h_("Ad Psychology",10,"adPsychology")
B.OQ=new A.as(61917,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.Nr=new A.br("rewarded_ads","Bribed Attention","Converts a commercial into a 'mission' that feels like part of the game loop, making the ad feel like progress rather than an interruption.","Mobile Gaming Industry (Early 2010s)","Only watch rewarded ads for games you truly enjoy and set a strict daily limit (e.g., 'max 3 ads') so advertisers do not control your playtime.",B.bQ,B.OQ,"Academic reviews of ad monetization in children's applications.","Analyses note rewarded ads heavily boost engagement because children focus on the immediate reward and often fail to recognize the persuasive intent.",!0)
B.OF=new A.as(59050,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.Ns=new A.br("advergames","Advergames","Builds an entire game around a brand, ensuring your fun and positive feelings transfer directly onto the product.","Branded Web Games (2000s)","Ask yourself: 'Would I still play this if the brand logo was removed?' If no, limit your time with it.",B.bQ,B.OF,"Research on children and advergames.","Children who play an advergame for a snack show significantly higher purchase intentions if they enjoy the game.",!0)
B.Nh=new A.br("in_game_placement","In-Game Placements","Embeds real-world brands into the game environment so you become accustomed to seeing them in fun and engaging contexts.","3D Online Gaming (2000s)","Spot the brands and ask: 'Is this here to make the world realistic, or did someone pay for this space?'",B.bQ,B.oV,"Experiments comparing in-game ads and advergames.","In-game ads raise purchase intentions by integrating brands seamlessly into enjoyable play.",!0)
B.Nu=new A.br("brand_mascots","Brand Mascots","Uses cute or human-like NPCs to trick your brain into treating them as trustworthy friends rather than corporate sales tools.","Classic Advertising to Digital NPCs","When a cute character recommends a purchase, picture the faceless corporate logo saying it instead to break the illusion.",B.bQ,B.oS,"Studies on brand anthropomorphism.","Giving brands human-like traits measurably increases perceived warmth and trust, boosting positive evaluations.",!0)
B.OC=new A.as(58978,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.Nc=new A.br("scarcity_timers","Scarcity Timers","Leverages the fear of missing out with fake deadlines or low stock warnings to push impulsive buying over careful thinking.","Retail Flash Sales to E-commerce","Never buy under a countdown. Take a screenshot, walk away, and wait 24 hours before deciding.",B.bQ,B.OC,"Behavioral psychology of scarcity.","Scarcity messages increase urgency and willingness to pay, heavily influencing targeted personality types.",!0)
B.Os=new A.as(58502,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.Ni=new A.br("social_proof_ads","Weaponized Social Proof","Claims a product is highly popular to make you assume it must be good and blindly copy the crowd.","E-commerce Ratings & Reviews","Ignore the popularity label entirely. Ask: 'Does this actually improve my experience for the price?'",B.bQ,B.Os,"Marketing studies on social proof.","Scarcity combined with social proof ('only 2 left, 1,500 bought') significantly speeds up checkout decisions.",!0)
B.OG=new A.as(59070,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.Nl=new A.br("native_ads","Stealth Native Ads","Designs ads to look exactly like regular posts or streams so your critical guard stays completely down.","Social Media Platforms (2010s)","Habitually scan for '#ad' or 'sponsored' tags, and always ask 'Who paid for this?' when watching influencers.",B.bQ,B.OG,"Studies on ad recognition and disclosure.","Only 17\u201327% of users correctly identify native ads as advertising, even with generic disclosure labels.",!0)
B.Na=new A.br("subliminal_priming","Subliminal Priming","Displays brief or subtle brand cues when you are vulnerable to secretly nudge your later choices.","Classic Lab Studies to Modern UI","When you suddenly crave a brand, trace it back. Did you just see it in a game? Naming the influence kills its power.",B.bQ,B.oR,"Neuroimaging work on dynamic food ads.","Dynamic brand ads activate brain reward regions more strongly than static images, bypassing conscious filtering.",!0)
B.O4=new A.as(57578,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.Nz=new A.br("halo_effect","The Halo Effect","Relies on a positive experience with one product to make you unconsciously assume everything else with that logo is equally good.","Classic Psychology","Evaluate every purchase on its own merits. Pretend the item has no brand name and check its actual features.",B.bQ,B.O4,"Marketing research on brand ecosystems.","A strong flagship product creates a psychological 'halo' that improves loyalty across entire brand ecosystems.",!0)
B.O3=new A.as(57567,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.N4=new A.br("neuromarketing","Neuromarketing","Advertisers use brain scans to find exactly which colors and sounds light up your reward circuits the most.","Biometric Ad Firms (2000s)","Feeling moved by an ad doesn't mean it's a good deal. Pause and check objective factors like price and utility.",B.bQ,B.O3,"Reviews of fMRI ad optimization.","Emotionally rich ads reliably activate the amygdala and insula, correlating directly with increased purchasing behavior.",!0)
